{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass\/step-swift.struct\/color"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct"]]},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLBassV4StepV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","title":"color"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct\/color","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBass/Step-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bass-step type represents the pitch step of the bass of the current chord within the harmony element. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text attribute indicates how the bass should appear in a score if not using the element contents."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Step","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Step","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass\/step-swift.struct","type":"topic","title":"MXLBass.Step"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBass":{"title":"MXLBass","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBass","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBass","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bass type is used to indicate a bass note in popular music chord symbols, e.g. G\/C. It is generally not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in functional harmony, as inversion is generally not used in pop chord symbols. As with root, it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"divided into step and alter elements, similar to pitches. The arrangement attribute specifies where the bass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is displayed relative to what precedes it."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","title":"MXLColor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBass/Step-swift.struct/color":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass\/step-swift.struct\/color","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct\/color","title":"color"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}